{
  "title": "Physical Quantities and Units",
  "order": 1,
  "pageType": "markdown",
  "content": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 1
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Physical Quantities and Units"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Introduction"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Physics is the study of the natural world, and to describe it accurately we need to measure things. A "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "physical quantity",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is any property that can be measured and expressed as a number with a unit. Understanding physical quantities and their units is fundamental to all of physics."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "blockquote",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Remember: ",
                "marks": [{ "type": "bold" }]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Every measurement in physics must include both a number and a unit. Writing '5' on its own is meaningless -- you must specify '5 metres', '5 seconds', or whatever quantity you are measuring."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Key Concepts"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What is a Physical Quantity?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A physical quantity consists of two parts:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "A "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "numerical value",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " (the magnitude)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "A "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "unit",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " (what is being measured)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "For example, a length of 5 metres has:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Numerical value: 5"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Unit: metres (m)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "SI Units (International System of Units)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Scientists worldwide use a standardised system called "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "SI units",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " (Système International). This ensures everyone uses the same measurements."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 4
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Base SI Units"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "codeBlock",
        "attrs": {
          "language": "text"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "| Quantity | Unit Name | Symbol |\n|----------|-----------|--------|\n| Length | metre | m |\n| Mass | kilogram | kg |\n| Time | second | s |\n| Electric current | ampere | A |\n| Temperature | kelvin | K |\n| Amount of substance | mole | mol |\n| Luminous intensity | candela | cd |"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "infoGrid",
        "attrs": {
          "title": "SI Base Units at a Glance",
          "columns": 2,
          "variant": "cards",
          "items": [
            {
              "title": "Length",
              "description": "Metre (m)",
              "color": "primary",
              "bullets": ["Base SI unit for distance", "1 km = 1000 m"]
            },
            {
              "title": "Mass",
              "description": "Kilogram (kg)",
              "color": "secondary",
              "bullets": ["Base SI unit (not the gram!)", "1 kg = 1000 g"]
            },
            {
              "title": "Time",
              "description": "Second (s)",
              "color": "primary",
              "bullets": ["Base SI unit for duration", "1 hour = 3600 s"]
            },
            {
              "title": "Electric Current",
              "description": "Ampere (A)",
              "color": "secondary",
              "bullets": ["Flow of electric charge", "Often shortened to 'amp'"]
            },
            {
              "title": "Temperature",
              "description": "Kelvin (K)",
              "color": "primary",
              "bullets": ["Absolute temperature scale", "0 K = -273.15 °C"]
            },
            {
              "title": "Amount of Substance",
              "description": "Mole (mol)",
              "color": "secondary",
              "bullets": ["Contains 6.02 x 10²³ particles", "Avogadro's number"]
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 4
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Derived Units"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Many units are combinations of base units:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "codeBlock",
        "attrs": {
          "language": "text"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "| Quantity | Unit | Symbol | In Base Units |\n|----------|------|--------|---------------|\n| Force | newton | N | kg·m/s² |\n| Energy | joule | J | kg·m²/s² |\n| Power | watt | W | kg·m²/s³ |\n| Pressure | pascal | Pa | kg/(m·s²) |\n| Frequency | hertz | Hz | 1/s |"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "SI Prefixes"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Prefixes are used to express very large or very small quantities:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "codeBlock",
        "attrs": {
          "language": "text"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "| Prefix | Symbol | Factor | Example |\n|--------|--------|--------|--------|\n| tera | T | $10^{12}$ | THz (terahertz) |\n| giga | G | $10^{9}$ | GW (gigawatt) |\n| mega | M | $10^{6}$ | MHz (megahertz) |\n| kilo | k | $10^{3}$ | km (kilometre) |\n| centi | c | $10^{-2}$ | cm (centimetre) |\n| milli | m | $10^{-3}$ | mm (millimetre) |\n| micro | μ | $10^{-6}$ | μm (micrometre) |\n| nano | n | $10^{-9}$ | nm (nanometre) |"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "blockquote",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Key Concept: ",
                "marks": [{ "type": "bold" }]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The SI system has seven base units (metre, kilogram, second, ampere, kelvin, mole, candela). All other units in physics are derived from combinations of these base units. For example, the newton (N) is equivalent to kg·m/s²."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "quizEmbed",
        "attrs": {
          "quizId": "check-physical-quantities"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Mathematical Relationships"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Converting Between Units"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "To convert between units, multiply or divide by the appropriate factor:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "codeBlock",
        "attrs": {
          "language": "math"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "1 \\text{ km} = 1000 \\text{ m} = 10^3 \\text{ m}"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "codeBlock",
        "attrs": {
          "language": "math"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "1 \\text{ mm} = 0.001 \\text{ m} = 10^{-3} \\text{ m}"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Standard Form"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Very large or small numbers are written in standard form:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "codeBlock",
        "attrs": {
          "language": "math"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "a \\times 10^n"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "1 \\leq a < 10",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "code"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " and "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "n",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "code"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is an integer."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Examples:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Speed of light: "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "3.0 \\times 10^8",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "code"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " m/s"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Electron mass: "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "9.1 \\times 10^{-31}",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "code"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " kg"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Worked Examples"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Example 1:",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " Convert 2.5 km to metres."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Solution:",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "codeBlock",
        "attrs": {
          "language": "math"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "2.5 \\text{ km} = 2.5 \\times 1000 \\text{ m} = 2500 \\text{ m}"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Example 2:",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " Convert 450 mm to metres."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Solution:",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "codeBlock",
        "attrs": {
          "language": "math"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "450 \\text{ mm} = 450 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{ m} = 0.45 \\text{ m}"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Example 3:",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " Express 0.000025 m in standard form and convert to micrometres."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Solution:",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " In standard form: "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "2.5 \\times 10^{-5}",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "code"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " m"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "In micrometres: "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "2.5 \\times 10^{-5} \\text{ m} = 25 \\text{ μm}",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "code"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "blockquote",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Common Mistake: ",
                "marks": [{ "type": "bold" }]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "When converting units, students often multiply when they should divide, or vice versa. Remember: converting to a smaller unit means the number gets bigger (e.g. 2.5 km = 2500 m), and converting to a larger unit means the number gets smaller (e.g. 450 mm = 0.45 m)."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "quizEmbed",
        "attrs": {
          "quizId": "check-physical-quantities-2"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Significant Figures"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Rules for Significant Figures"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "All non-zero digits are significant: 123 has 3 s.f."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Zeros between non-zero digits are significant: 102 has 3 s.f."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Leading zeros are not significant: 0.0025 has 2 s.f."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Trailing zeros after a decimal point are significant: 2.50 has 3 s.f."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Calculations with Significant Figures"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Your answer should have the same number of significant figures as the least precise measurement used."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Real-World Applications"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Engineering:",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " Precise measurements in construction and manufacturing"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Medicine:",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " Drug dosages measured in milligrams or micrograms"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Astronomy:",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " Distances measured in kilometres, light-years, or parsecs"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Electronics:",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " Component values in microfarads, nanohenries"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Common Misconceptions"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "\"Weight is measured in kilograms\"",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " — Weight is a force, measured in newtons (N). Mass is measured in kilograms."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "\"Centi means one hundredth everywhere\"",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " — It does! 1 cm = 0.01 m, but students often forget this when converting."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "\"More decimal places means more accurate\"",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " — Precision is not the same as accuracy. A measurement can be precise but inaccurate."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Practice Problems"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Calculate the result of converting 3.2 km to: a) metres b) centimetres c) millimetres"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
